@startuml release-train
'==============================================================================
' Figure (Chapter I): the release-train delivery model.
' Three scope-sized PRODUCT phases with absolute gates (all realised), then a
' fourth, different kind of work: a planned engineering effort on the
' event-sourced system (designed, not shipped as a customer release).
' Realised vs planned is also carried in the figure caption. From the
' methodology section (release-train delivery).
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg release-train.puml  then  rsvg-convert -f pdf
'==============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor Black
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor<<planned>> Gray
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> #F5F5F5
  BorderStyle<<planned>> dashed
}

rectangle "Phase 0  --  Engineering foundations\n(repository, CI/CD, dev environment, roadmap)" as p0
rectangle "Phase 1  --  MVP, full stack\n(registry, document links, deadlines,\napprovals, dashboard, IAM)" as p1
rectangle "Phase 2  --  Enterprise features\n(intelligence-assisted extraction, e-signature,\ncustom fields, obligations, advanced reporting)" as p2
rectangle "Improvements in the event-sourced system\n(broker-communication, multi-tenancy,\nscalability of comby and the event store)" as ev <<Part 2>>

p0 --> p1 : gate
p1 --> p2 : gate
p2 ..> ev : designed,\nnot shipped

note bottom of p2
  Phases 0--2 realised and
  shipped to production.
end note
@enduml
